---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro'
import PageHead from '@/components/PageHead.astro'
import { SITE, SOCIAL_LINKS } from '@/consts'
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components'

// Get contact email from social links
const contactEmail =
  SOCIAL_LINKS.find((link) => link.label === 'Email')?.href.replace(
    'mailto:',
    '',
  ) || 'your@email.com'
const siteName = SITE.title
---

<Layout class="max-w-3xl">
  <PageHead slot="head" title="Privacy Policy" />
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy', icon: 'lucide:shield-check' }]}
  />

  <article class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <div class="bg-card/50 mb-6 rounded-lg border p-6">
      <div class="mb-2 flex items-center gap-3">
        <Icon name="lucide:shield-check" class="text-primary size-6" />
        <h1 class="m-0 text-3xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground m-0 text-sm">
        Last updated: {
          new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-CA', {
            year: 'numeric',
            month: 'long',
            day: 'numeric',
          })
        }
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">About This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        My name is <strong>Andrew Raisbeck</strong> and {siteName}
        (andrewraisbeck.com) is my personal portfolio and blog. This policy
        explains what personal information I collect through this site, why I
        collect it, how it is handled, and the choices you have.
      </p>
      <p>
        I try to collect as little information as possible. I do not sell your
        personal information, and I do not run third-party advertising or
        analytics on this site. If that ever changes, I will update this page
        and, where the law requires it, ask for your consent first.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Consent</h2>
      <p>
        I am located in Ontario, Canada. This policy is written to meet my
        obligations under Canada's <em>Personal Information Protection and
        Electronic Documents Act</em> (PIPEDA) and — for emails I send —
        Canada's <em>Anti-Spam Legislation</em> (CASL).
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Implied consent</strong> covers the routine, low-risk data
          described below (for example, server request logs and your browser's
          own storage of your theme preference). By using the site, you
          reasonably expect this.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Express consent</strong> is required for my email newsletter.
          You are only added to the newsletter if you deliberately check the
          consent box in the sign-up form <em>and</em> confirm your
          subscription by clicking the link in the confirmation email
          (double opt-in). I keep a record of that confirmation as proof of
          consent, as CASL requires.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can withdraw your consent at any time — for the newsletter by
        unsubscribing (every email contains a working unsubscribe link), and
        for anything else by contacting me. Withdrawing consent will not
        affect the lawfulness of anything done before you withdrew it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What I Collect, and Why</h2>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">1. Newsletter (Brevo)</h3>
      <p>When you subscribe to my newsletter, I collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your email address</strong> — so I can send the newsletter
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Subscription metadata</strong> — for example, when you
          subscribed and your current subscription status
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proof of consent</strong> — Brevo's double opt-in process
          records the date, time, and originating IP address of your
          confirmation click, so I can demonstrate that valid consent existed
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I use <strong>Brevo</strong> (formerly Sendinblue) to store subscriber
        emails and send the newsletter. Brevo processes this information on my
        behalf as my service provider; see Brevo's
        <a
          href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="underline">Privacy Policy</a
        > for details.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Legal basis:</strong> your express consent (CASL; PIPEDA
        consent requirement)<br />
        <strong>Retention:</strong> until you unsubscribe or ask me to delete
        it. If you unsubscribe, I keep a minimal suppression record (your email
        address marked unsubscribed) so you are not accidentally re-added.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">2. Comments (giscus / GitHub)</h3>
      <p>
        Comments on my blog posts use <strong>giscus</strong>, an open-source
        commenting widget backed by <strong>GitHub Discussions</strong>. If you
        leave a comment, you sign in with your GitHub account and the comment
        is stored publicly in the GitHub repository that powers this site.
        Specifically:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your GitHub username, avatar, and any public profile information
          GitHub shares with the widget
        </li>
        <li>The content of your comment and its timestamps</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data is processed by
        <a
          href="https://giscus.app"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="underline">giscus</a
        > and <a
          href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/github-privacy-statement"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="underline">GitHub</a
        > under their own privacy policies, and remains subject to GitHub's
        terms since it lives in a GitHub repository. Participating in comments
        is entirely optional.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Legal basis:</strong> your consent when you choose to comment<br />
        <strong>Retention:</strong> for as long as you keep the comment posted
        on GitHub; delete your comment (or ask me to) to remove it
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">3. Hosting and Security (Cloudflare)</h3>
      <p>
        This site is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong>. Like virtually
        all web hosts, Cloudflare processes standard request metadata — for
        example your IP address, browser user-agent, and the time of your
        request — to deliver the site, protect it from abuse and attacks, and
        keep it working. I do not use this data to profile individuals.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Legal basis:</strong> my legitimate interest in operating and
        securing the site (implied consent)<br />
        <strong>Retention:</strong> handled by Cloudflare under its
        <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="underline">Privacy Policy</a
        >, using short retention periods
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">4. Data Stored in Your Browser</h3>
      <p>
        When you toggle the light/dark theme switch, your choice is saved in
        your browser's <code>localStorage</code> so the theme persists between
        visits. This stays entirely on your device; I never receive it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Optional Features (Currently Disabled)</h2>
      <p>
        The following third-party features exist in the site's code but are
        <strong>not currently active</strong>. If I enable any of them, I will
        update this page first and, where required, obtain your consent:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics</strong> — optional Google Analytics or Umami
          analytics could measure aggregate traffic. Neither is enabled.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Advertising</strong> — an optional Google AdSense integration
          could display ads. It is not enabled. If I ever enable personalized
          ads, I will present appropriate consent controls before those cookies
          are set, as Google's requirements and applicable privacy law demand.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets <strong>no first-party tracking cookies</strong>. In
        summary:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Strictly necessary / local:</strong> theme preference saved
          in your browser's localStorage (your device only)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Comment widget:</strong> the giscus iframe and GitHub may use
          cookies or similar technologies to operate the comments feature
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting:</strong> Cloudflare may use strictly necessary
          cookies or headers to serve and secure the site
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Advertising / analytics cookies:</strong> none, while these
          features are disabled
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can clear or block cookies and site data through your browser
        settings at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Who I Share Information With</h2>
      <p>I do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. I share it only with these service providers, strictly as needed to run the site:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Brevo</strong> — newsletter delivery and subscriber storage —
          <a
            href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline">Privacy Policy</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub</strong> — comment storage (Discussions) — <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/github-privacy-statement"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline">Privacy Statement</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — web hosting, content delivery, and
          security — <a
            href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline">Privacy Policy</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I may also disclose information where required by law (for example, a
        court order or valid legal process).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Your Rights (Canada)</h2>
      <p>Under PIPEDA and provincial privacy law, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Access</strong> the personal information I hold about you
          (within 30 days of your request, as PIPEDA requires)
        </li>
        <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate information</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> (for example, unsubscribe from the
          newsletter) and expect it to take effect promptly — CASL requires
          unsubscribe requests to be honoured within <strong>10 business
          days</strong>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Complain</strong> about how I handle your information; please
          contact me first and I will respond. You may also contact the
          <a
            href="https://www.priv.gc.ca/en/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline">Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada</a
          >, or — for spam concerns — the
          <a
            href="https://crtc.gc.ca/eng/com500/faq500.htm"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline">CRTC</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you are visiting from the European Economic Area or the United
        Kingdom: where optional features that would affect you are enabled, you
        have corresponding rights under the GDPR (access, rectification,
        erasure, restriction, portability, objection, and the right to withdraw
        consent). Contact me any time to exercise these rights.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">About the Newsletter Emails</h2>
      <p>
        What subscribers receive: emails referencing new blog posts and,
        occasionally, notable updates to the site — nothing else. Every email:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Identifies me as the sender (name, with my contact details)</li>
        <li>Explains why you are receiving it</li>
        <li>
          Includes a working unsubscribe link, honoured within 10 business days
          as CASL requires
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you believe you received a commercial email from me without consent,
        please contact me directly — or use the unsubscribe link — and I will
        sort it out promptly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">How Your Information Is Protected</h2>
      <p>
        I protect personal information with security measures appropriate to
        its sensitivity: the site is served over HTTPS, the subscription
        endpoint validates input and stores nothing locally, and no personally
        identifying records are kept on the site itself — subscriber data lives
        with Brevo, comments live with GitHub. No method of transmission over
        the Internet is 100% secure, so I cannot promise absolute security, but
        I will notify affected individuals and the Privacy Commissioner of
        Canada of any privacy breach involving sensitive information, as
        required by law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a professional portfolio and blog, and is not directed at
        children. I do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone
        under 13 (and do not knowingly seek newsletter sign-ups under 16). If
        you believe a child has provided personal information, contact me and
        I will delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        I may update this policy from time to time — for example, if I enable
        analytics or advertising, or change newsletter providers. The version
        posted here with its "Last updated" date is always the current one.
        Material changes affecting previously collected, consented-to
        information (such as the newsletter list) may also be announced in the
        newsletter itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Contact Me</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, access requests, corrections, or complaints: I am the
        person accountable for personal information on this site.
      </p>
      <div class="bg-muted/30 rounded-lg border p-4">
        <p class="m-0">
          <strong>Andrew Raisbeck</strong><br />
          <strong>Email:</strong>
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="underline">{contactEmail}</a
          >
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground m-0 mt-2 text-sm">
          I aim to respond within 30 days, as PIPEDA requires.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
